          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The concept of a
            %em causal complement
            is suitable to establish a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+disjointness+relation"} causal disjointness relation
            on index sets where the indices are subsets of a given set. This generalizes the concept of causal complement of subsets of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haag-Kastler+vacuum+representation"} Haag-Kastler vacuum representation
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The concept of causal complement, as the name indicates, a concept related to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causality"} causality
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetimes"} spacetimes
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentzian+manifolds"} Lorentzian manifolds
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a{:href => "#OnLorentzianManifolds"} On Lorentzian manifolds
              \.
          %p One may abstract away some of the key properties of causal complements on Lorentzian manifolds to obtain a more general concept:
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#AbstractDefinition"} Abstract definition
          %h3#OnLorentzianManifolds On Lorentzian manifolds
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentzian+manifold"} Lorentzian manifold
            (a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+manifold"} pseudo-Riemannian manifold
            with one
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time-like"} time-like
            dimension in each tangent space.
          %p
            Then for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset X
            any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+cone"} causal cone
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J(S)
            is the subset of all points in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            which may be joined to a point of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curve"} curve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma \colon [0,1] \to X
            which is everywere
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/timelike"} timelike
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lightlike"} lightlike
          #CausalComplementOfSubsetOfLorentzianManifold.num_example
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (causal complement of subset of Lorentzian manifold)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
              of a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentzian+manifold"} Lorentzian manifold
              %em causal complement
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mo ⊥
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^\perp
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
              of the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+cone"} causal cone
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mo ⊥
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∖
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^\perp \;\coloneqq\; X \setminus J(S)
                    \\,.
            %p
              The causal complement
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊥
                        %mo ⊥
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{\perp \perp}
              of the causal complement
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mo ⊥
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^\perp
              is called the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+closure"} causal closure
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊥
                        %mo ⊥
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S = S^{\perp \perp}
            %p
              then the subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is called a
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causally+closed+subset"} causally closed subset
          %h3#AbstractDefinition Abstract definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be an arbitrary set and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \subset X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mo ⊥
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M \mapsto M^{\perp} \subset X
          %p
            is called a
            %strong causal complement
            if the following conditions hold:
          %p
            (i)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo ⊆
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊥
                      %mo ⊥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \subseteq M^{\perp\perp}
          %p
            (ii)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                    %mi j
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi j
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊥
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi j
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\bigcup_j M_j)^{\perp} = \bigcap_j (M_j)^{\perp}
          %p
            (iii)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mo ⊥
                  %mo =
                  %mi ∅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \bigcap M^{\perp} = \emptyset
          %p
            A set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causally+closed+subset"} causally closed
            iff
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi M
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊥
                        %mo ⊥
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M = M^{\perp\perp}
          %p
            The set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊥
                      %mo ⊥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^{\perp\perp}
            is the
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+closure"} causal closure
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p Causal complements are always causally closed. The intersection of two causally closed sets is again a causally closed set. The causal complement of a set may be empty.
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+disjointness+relation"} causal disjointness relation
            on an index set of subsets of a given set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            can be defined via
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⊥
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mtext iff
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M_1 \perp M_2 \; \text{iff} \; M_1 \subseteq (M_2)^{\perp}
          %p
            if all sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            have a causal complement and if
          %p
            (iv) there is a sequence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mi n
                  %msubsup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y_n)_{n=1}^{\infty}
            of mutually different subsets with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi n
                    %mo ⊥
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi ∅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_n^{\perp} \neq \emptyset
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcup Y_n = X
          %p
            The latter condition is needed to get a
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              \-bounded
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            = succeed "-boundedness" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+index+set"} causal index set
